.5 and the highest weight of 0.57, supported by a real PSF-like stamp detection with p_real 0.82. The red g-r color near peak is self-consistently explained as a reddened broad Ia with x1 of 2.57 and c of 0.37.", "hypothesis": "ia", "refuted_if": {"band": "ztfr", "day": 5, "direction": "above", "flux": 200, "why": "Eight and a half days after Ia maximum the r band must have faded well below peak so sustained peak-level flux would rule out the Ia decline"}, "weakest_point": "The fit sits at the extreme broad and red edge of the Ia population with only one g-band detection constraining color and a flat r-band top from day -3.5 to -0.5."}, {"argument": "The 15-day slow r-band rise from 18.45 to 18.0 mag with red g-r near 0.85 mag fits a luminous stripped-envelope supernova near maximum with chi2 per point 0.75 at z=0.096. Deep pre-explosion limits to 20 mag plus a real central PSF stamp with p_real 0.82 support a new explosive transient.", "hypothesis": "ibc", "refuted_if": {"band": "ztfr", "day": 5, "direction": "above", "flux": 200, "why": "At about 31 days after the fitted Ib/c peak the light curve must be fading on the cobalt tail, so sustained brightness near 220 uJy rules out decline."}, "weakest_point": "The fit puts peak at day -26.5, eleven days before the first detection, leaving the rise unseen while the observed late brightening conflicts with post-peak decline."}, {"argument": "The ~15-day nearly flat r-band detections from 18.45 to 18.04 mag after a month of deep non-detections match a hydrogen-rich plateau at z~0.09 caught after rise. The red g-r ~0.85 mag near day -4 and a real PSF-like difference source with p_real 0.82 support a slowly evolving cool photosphere rather than an artifact.", "hypothesis": "ii", "refuted_if": {"band": "ztfr", "day": 5, "direction": "below", "flux": 140, "why": "A Type II plateau cannot fade by ~0.5 mag in five days, so such a drop would require a fast-declining rival rather than a plateau."}, "weakest_point": "The II fit has chi2 per point 6.88 and weight 0.18% far below Ia and Ibc, because its predicted peak at -21.6 d coincides with a deep g limit of 19.9 mag."}], "weights": {"ia": 0.7423, "ibc": 0.1272, "ii": 0.0007, "null": 0.1298}, "wording": {"term": "about as likely as not", "text": "It is about as likely as not that the distant flash will still look bright in red light five days from now.", "words_match": true}}, "prev": "2d73c6d8dd8ccf5e93fa0d015e6a155ba25d8421b4f5da90b40f2ac2d01d2108", "seq": 10, "time": "2021-04-09T22:32:26+00:00", "v": 2}
